ys","quantity":1}]}}],"rulesText":"By Inferno's Light (Introduction)\n\nMap and mission parameters, p. 6\n\nBriefing: Ambush the Dominion supply convoy travelling from the wormhole toward Cardassia.\n\nMap: Two player deployment corners (upper left and lower right); each player chooses either. Place two freighters per player in the upper-right arrangements marked for that player count, facing point E at lower left. The initial Dominion wing is at C, also facing E. Randomly place four asteroids in the indicated interior area, at least Range 1 apart. Top/right edges are Dominion; bottom/left edges are Federation Alliance. See the exact diagram on p. 6.\n\nObjective: Destroy at least one freighter per player. If more freighters than the player count escape, fail immediately. If all freighters are destroyed, players still must retreat to end the mission. Failure replays this mission; success proceeds to Call to Arms.\n\nXP and deadline: 1 XP each for destroying at least one freighter per player; +1 XP each if all are destroyed. Destroyed players receive 1 fewer XP, minimum 0. Retreat is allowed through either Alliance edge. End Round 10 automatically retreats remaining players.\n\n Formation  Round  Bearing  Orders  2p  3p  4p  5p  6p \n---------------------------\n Dominion 1st Wing  Setup  C  Attack  AS-D  AS-D  -  AS-D  - \n Dominion Alpha  2  Roll  Attack  AS-E  -  AS-E  -  - \n Dominion 2nd Wing  3  Roll  Attack  AS  AS  -  AS  AS \n Cardassian Glinn  4  Roll  Attack  G  -  G  -  - \n Cardassian Gul  6  Roll  Attack  G-E  -  -  G-E  - \n\nFreighters: Treat as based ships for overlap. Attack 1, Agility 1, Hull 3, Shields 0. Each uncancelled critical counts as two hits. Start Activation, before other movement, move freighters nearest E first. Roll a defense die for each: evade = speed 2 straight; battle stations = speed 3 straight; blank = speed 2 bank left/right, whichever ends nearest a Dominion edge (random tie). Freighters do not swerve around asteroids. A completed maneuver without overlap grants a battle-stations token. End Combat, each attacks the nearest player ship in arc. Leaving a Dominion edge escapes.\n\nOptional introductory builds (all Skill 4): K'Vort: (1) Helmsman, Reactor Vent, Reckless Assault; (2) Operations Officer, Secondary Cloaking Coil, Strafing Run; (3) Glory to the Empire, Torpedo Fusillade, Weapons Officer. Vor'cha: (1) Converging Fire, First Officer, Targeting Array; (2) Eye for an Eye, Forward Battery, Reinforced Hull, with 1 XP left; (3) Glory to the Empire!, Photon Torpedoes, Science Officer, Secondary Relays.\n\n","manualRules":["Resolve special movement, target orders, objectives, XP, penalties and retreat manually. See the Rules card."]},"A4M2":{"id":"A4M2","name":"Alliance Act IV - Call to Arms","book2":true,"act":4,"maxRound":12,"sourcePages":[8,9],"profiles":{"ASR":{"className":"Jem'Hadar Attack Ship","definitionId":"S301","skill":1,"shields":2,"hull":3,"cardId":"285600","advanced":false,"description":"Book II Regular | Skill 1 | Hull 3 | Shields 2. Resolve printed card abilities manually. Starting stats follow user settings; printed bonus shields do not change these starting counts."},"ASE":{"className":"Jem'Hadar Attack Ship","definitionId":"S301","skill":4,"shields":2,"hull":3,"cardId":"325000","advanced":true,"description":"Book II Elite | Skill 4 | Hull 3 | Shields 2. Resolve printed card abilities manually. Starting stats follow user settings; printed bonus shields do not change these starting counts."},"GR":{"className":"Cardassian Galor Class","definitionId":"S334","skill":2,"shields":3,"hull":4,"cardId":"288300","advanced":false,"description":"Book II Regular | Skill 2 | Hull 4 | Shields 3. Resolve printed card abilities manually. Starting stats follow user settings; printed bonus shields do not change these starting counts."},"GE":{"className":"Cardassian Galor Class","definitionId":"S334","skill":5,"shields":3,"hull":4,"cardId":"288300","advanced":true,"description":"Book II Elit