ty":2}],"4":[{"ship_class":"G","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}],"6":[{"ship_class":"G","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}]},"bearing":6},{"id":"wave2","name":"Dominion 1st Wing","round":2,"orders":"Hunt","hardOnly":false,"columns":{"2":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}],"3":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}],"6":[{"ship_class":"BC","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}]}},{"id":"wave3","name":"Dominion 2nd Wing","round":3,"orders":"Hunt","hardOnly":false,"columns":{"2":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}],"4":[{"ship_class":"BC","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}],"5":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}]}},{"id":"wave4","name":"Dominion 3rd Wing","round":4,"orders":"Hunt","hardOnly":false,"columns":{"2":[{"ship_class":"BC","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}],"4":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}],"6":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"regular","quantity":1}]}},{"id":"wave5","name":"Dominion Alpha","round":6,"orders":"Hunt","hardOnly":false,"columns":{"2":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"difficulty_only","quantity":1}],"3":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"always","quantity":1}],"5":[{"ship_class":"AS","elite":"always","quantity":1}]}}],"rulesText":"Invasion of Betazed (Finale)\n\nMap and mission parameters, p. 18\n\nBriefing: Cover the outnumbered Tenth Fleet's withdrawal from Betazed.\n\nMap: Players deploy in the bottom strip. Planet is above/right of center. Randomly place three asteroids in the marked right-side area, at least Range 1 from other obstacles and the planet. One Miranda per player uses the printed left-side sites/facings: two base positions, then added sites at 3p, 4p, 5p and 6p. Bottom/right are Alliance edges; top/left are Dominion. Initial Galors enter bearing 6.\n\nObjective: At least half the Mirandas, rounded up, must survive and escape through an Alliance edge. Success wins the campaign; failure loses it.\n\nXP and deadline: Each player receives 1 XP, plus 1 per BC destroyed. Destroyed players receive 1 fewer, printed minimum 1. Players must retreat through an Alliance edge by end Round 10; remaining players are destroyed then. The deadline sentence explicitly says players; the book does not separately state what happens to Mirandas still on the board at that instant.\n\n Formation  Round  Bearing  Orders  2p  3p  4p  5p  6p \n---------------------------\n Cardassian Glinn  Setup  6  Attack  2 G-D  -  G-D  -  G-D \n Dominion 1st Wing  2  Roll  Hunt  AS  AS  -  -  BC-D \n Dominion 2nd Wing  3  Roll  Hunt  AS  -  BC-D  AS  - \n Dominion 3rd Wing  4  Roll  Hunt  BC-D  -  AS  -  AS \n Dominion Alpha  6  Roll  Hunt  AS-D  AS-E  -  AS-E  - \n\nMirandas: One per player. Attack 2, Agility 2, Shields 0. Hull depends on Act V Dominion Influence: 0 = Hull 3; 1 = Hull 4; 2 = Hull 5. This direction is as printed. Treat as based ships. Uncancelled criticals against them count as two hits.\n\nMovement/actions: Start Activation at Captain Skill 0, players move each Miranda with speed 2 or 3, using hard turn left, bank left, straight, bank right, or hard turn right. After a successfully completed maneuver, players may give it a battle-stations or evade token. Leaving an Alliance edge escapes.\n\nAttacks: End Combat, each Miranda may attack a target in its front 180-degree arc.\n\nHunt: Upon deployment, before Planning, each Hunt ship immediately executes a straight maneuver with speed equal to the current round number (therefore includes speed 6 arrivals). Thereafter maneuvers target the nearest Miranda. Attack the closest legal Miranda, except when the nearest Miranda is beyond Range 1, another legal Range 1 target may be attacked. If no Tenth Fleet ships remain in play, change to Attack orders.\n\n","manualRules":["Resolve special movement, target orders, objectives, XP, penalties and retreat manually. See the Rules card."]}}]========])
for id,d in pairs(definitions) do STA2E_MISSION_DEFINITIONS[id]=d end
